1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:05,710
A workflow runs because something happens, does its work in tasks, and moves

2
00:00:05,710 --> 00:00:08,754
from one activity to the next through outcomes.

3
00:00:08,754 --> 00:00:13,004
In this video, you build a workflow that reacts to a published page,

4
00:00:13,004 --> 00:00:16,220
and learn what each of these building blocks does.

5
00:00:20,820 --> 00:00:24,440
A workflow is a set of activities connected to each other.

6
00:00:24,440 --> 00:00:28,117
An event is an activity that waits for something to happen.

7
00:00:28,117 --> 00:00:33,490
As the start activity, it starts the workflow; anywhere else, it makes the workflow wait.

8
00:00:34,240 --> 00:00:38,922
A task is an activity that does something, such as showing a notification,

9
00:00:38,922 --> 00:00:41,614
writing to the log, or sending an email.

10
00:00:41,614 --> 00:00:44,540
The workflow runs a task when it reaches it.

11
00:00:45,290 --> 00:00:49,508
An outcome tells the workflow how an activity ended, such as Done.

12
00:00:49,508 --> 00:00:52,144
Some activities offer several outcomes:

13
00:00:52,144 --> 00:00:56,830
an If Else Task has True and False, and an Email Task has Done and Failed.

14
00:00:57,580 --> 00:01:01,895
You connect an outcome to the next activity, and the connection tells the

15
00:01:01,895 --> 00:01:03,642
workflow what to run next.

16
00:01:03,642 --> 00:01:07,520
An activity that no connection reaches from the start never runs.

17
00:01:11,738 --> 00:01:14,774
Workflows are under Design in the admin menu.

18
00:01:14,774 --> 00:01:19,538
Let's open Workflows, where the list is empty, and select Create Workflow.

19
00:01:20,054 --> 00:01:21,982
A workflow only needs a name.

20
00:01:21,982 --> 00:01:26,554
Let's type Announce published pages, and select Create and open the designer.

21
00:01:27,013 --> 00:01:29,701
The designer opens on an empty canvas.

22
00:01:29,701 --> 00:01:34,588
A workflow runs when something happens, so it offers events to start with.

23
00:01:34,588 --> 00:01:37,093
Let's pick Content Published Event.

24
00:01:37,591 --> 00:01:41,369
The event appears on the canvas with a Start badge, because the first

25
00:01:41,369 --> 00:01:43,736
event you add becomes the start activity.

26
00:01:43,736 --> 00:01:45,651
Its settings open at the bottom.

27
00:01:46,123 --> 00:01:48,429
Content Types filters the event.

28
00:01:48,429 --> 00:01:53,103
Let's select Page, so that only publishing a page starts this workflow.

29
00:01:57,393 --> 00:02:01,385
The event has one outcome, Done, shown as a port on the right

30
00:02:01,385 --> 00:02:02,994
edge of the activity.

31
00:02:02,994 --> 00:02:06,391
Pointing at a port that leads nowhere shows a plus.

32
00:02:06,391 --> 00:02:07,643
Let's click it.

33
00:02:08,095 --> 00:02:12,261
A menu lists the activities you can add next, and you can search it.

34
00:02:12,261 --> 00:02:15,075
Let's search for fork, and select Fork Task.

35
00:02:15,575 --> 00:02:19,093
The Fork Task is added to the right, already connected.

36
00:02:19,093 --> 00:02:22,438
The line between the two activities is a connection:

37
00:02:22,438 --> 00:02:26,995
when the event finishes with Done, the workflow goes on to the Fork Task.

38
00:02:27,448 --> 00:02:33,214
Some activities have fixed outcomes, but a Fork Task takes its outcomes from its settings.

39
00:02:33,214 --> 00:02:36,336
In Forks, you enter names separated by commas.

40
00:02:36,336 --> 00:02:38,318
Let's enter Editors, Audit.

41
00:02:38,788 --> 00:02:42,400
The Fork Task shows two outcomes, Editors and Audit.

42
00:02:42,400 --> 00:02:48,628
When it runs, the workflow follows both of them, so each outcome can lead somewhere different.

43
00:02:52,928 --> 00:02:57,931
Let's click the Editors outcome, search for notify, and select Notify Task.

44
00:02:57,931 --> 00:03:01,328
A task is where the work of the workflow happens.

45
00:03:01,815 --> 00:03:05,292
Notify Task has a Notification Type and a Message.

46
00:03:05,292 --> 00:03:07,466
Let's keep Success, and type:

47
00:03:07,466 --> 00:03:10,819
Announced by the workflow, a page was published.

48
00:03:10,819 --> 00:03:13,985
The activity on the canvas shows the message.

49
00:03:14,441 --> 00:03:18,604
For the Audit outcome, let's use the Activities pane on the left.

50
00:03:18,604 --> 00:03:22,651
Search for log, select Tasks to keep only tasks, and click Log.

51
00:03:27,081 --> 00:03:30,185
Log Task writes a line to the log of the site.

52
00:03:30,185 --> 00:03:33,111
Let's keep the Information level, and type:

53
00:03:33,111 --> 00:03:35,141
Audit, a page was published.

54
00:03:35,607 --> 00:03:38,292
A badge on the Log Task counts its issues.

55
00:03:38,292 --> 00:03:39,859
This one is a warning:

56
00:03:39,859 --> 00:03:43,887
nothing connects the task to the start activity, so it never runs.

57
00:03:44,369 --> 00:03:47,599
Let's drag from the Audit outcome onto Log Task.

58
00:03:47,599 --> 00:03:50,949
The connection is drawn, and the badge disappears.

59
00:03:53,093 --> 00:03:56,716
Notify Task and Log Task each have one outcome, Done.

60
00:03:56,716 --> 00:04:01,445
Nothing is connected to it, so each branch ends there, and the workflow

61
00:04:01,445 --> 00:04:03,533
finishes once both have run.

62
00:04:07,769 --> 00:04:11,939
The designer saves your changes to a draft, and a draft does not run.

63
00:04:11,939 --> 00:04:14,496
Select Publish to make the workflow run.

64
00:04:14,496 --> 00:04:18,499
The version shown in the toolbar changes to the one you published.

65
00:04:18,958 --> 00:04:20,477
Let's publish a page.

66
00:04:20,477 --> 00:04:25,428
Under Content, Content Items, the New menu lists the content types you can create.

67
00:04:25,428 --> 00:04:26,778
Let's choose Page.

68
00:04:27,239 --> 00:04:31,341
Let's type Opening hours as the title, and select Publish.

69
00:04:31,341 --> 00:04:35,379
Publishing a page is the event that starts this workflow.

70
00:04:35,864 --> 00:04:39,720
The list comes back with the notification of the Notify Task, next to

71
00:04:39,720 --> 00:04:42,084
the message that the page was published.

72
00:04:42,552 --> 00:04:46,787
To check what ran, let's open Instances from the Workflows page.

73
00:04:46,787 --> 00:04:51,022
Each run of a workflow is an instance, and this one is Finished.

74
00:04:51,478 --> 00:04:53,221
Let's open the instance.

75
00:04:53,221 --> 00:04:57,170
The canvas highlights the activities and connections that ran:

76
00:04:57,170 --> 00:05:00,074
the event, the Fork Task, and both branches.

77
00:05:00,074 --> 00:05:02,978
A separate video covers instances in detail.

78
00:05:04,978 --> 00:05:08,874
An event starts a workflow or makes it wait, tasks do the work,

79
00:05:08,874 --> 00:05:11,810
and outcomes connect one activity to the next.

80
00:05:11,810 --> 00:05:13,278
Thanks for watching.

